        ("Prizes and government allowances", "\"Congratulations, you won!\" or \"Tap this link to get your allowance.\"", "Do not tap unknown links. You never need a fee or PIN to receive a prize or allowance, and you never send money first."),
        ("\"Your account will be blocked\"", "\"Update your KYC now or your account will be blocked.\"", "Call the official hotline yourself, not the number in the message."),
        ("A fake fine or legal notice", "A message in the name of BRTA or the police: a vehicle fine is due, a link to pay, a short deadline and a threat of a case, sometimes a discount for paying fast.", "Do not pay through the link. Open the official website yourself or ask the office. The deadline and the threat are the scammer's pressure."),
        ("Earn from home, but pay a fee first", "A group or app promises daily income for simple tasks, then asks for an activation, verification or withdrawal fee, and then another payment.", "A real platform does not charge you to withdraw your own money. Stop at the first fee; asking again is the sign."),
        ("A courier or parcel fee", "\"Your parcel is held, pay a redelivery fee\", often with a link, and more money later for a \"server error\". It can follow an online shop that took a small advance.", "Call the courier on its official number. Do not pay repeated charges; the parcel may be only an excuse."),
        ("A call or message from the police or 999", "Someone says a case has been filed against you, then asks for money, your PIN or bank details, or tells you to call a number.", "999 and the police never ask for a PIN or bank details. Hang up and call 999 or your station yourself. The number on the screen can be faked."),
